 We too: we (LibRaw team) focused on RAW decode and metadata extraction, but not
 on postprocessing (demosaic, noise suppression, etc).
 
-So, LibRaw-demosaic-pack-GPLn are abandoned now. We will be happy to convey 
+So, LibRaw-demosaic-pack-GPLn are abandoned now. We will be happy to convey
 their support and development to any developer who will show interest.
 
 LibRaw 0.19 contains callback calls placed instead of calls to demosaic pack routines.
 So, adaptation of demosaic packs to new LibRaw should be easy (and, of course, we'll
 provide some support and/or implement additional callbacks if needed).
 
+======================= Building with the demosaic packs =====================
 
-                                                              
+This tree can again be built with the (unmodified) last released packs,
+LibRaw-demosaic-pack-GPL2-0.18.8 and LibRaw-demosaic-pack-GPL3-0.18.8
+(https://www.libraw.org/data/). The glue code is in
+src/demosaic/demosaic_packs.cpp; it contains no GPL code and compiles to
+nothing unless a pack is enabled.
+
+LICENSE WARNING: a library built with the GPL2 pack is covered by the GPL
+version 2 or later; with the GPL3 pack, by the GPL version 3 or later.
+Without the packs, LibRaw stays LGPL 2.1 / CDDL 1.0.
+
+Algorithms (imgdata.params.user_qual, dcraw_emu -q):
+   5  AHD-Mod   modified AHD (Paul Lee)                     GPL2 pack
+   6  AFD       Adaptive Filtered Demosaic (5-pass)         GPL2 pack
+   7  VCD       Variance of Color Differences               GPL2 pack
+   8  VCD+AHD   mixed VCD/modified AHD                      GPL2 pack
+                (uses median_filter_new() when med_passes > 0)
+   9  LMMSE     LMMSE interpolation                         GPL2 pack
+  10  AMaZE     AMaZE (from RawTherapee)                    GPL3 pack
+Without the corresponding pack these fall back to AHD and set
+LIBRAW_WARN_FALLBACK_TO_AHD in imgdata.process_warnings, as before.
+
+The other pack features of LibRaw 0.18 (CA correction, line/impulse noise
+reduction, green equilibration, the GPL2 Foveon decoder, VCD refinement and
+edge-sensitive median filter) are not available: their parameters no longer
+exist in libraw_output_params_t.
+
+Run-time detection:
+  LibRaw::capabilities() / libraw_capabilities() report
+  LIBRAW_CAPS_DEMOSAICSGPL2 and LIBRAW_CAPS_DEMOSAICSGPL3.
+  libraw_const.h defines LIBRAW_HAS_DEMOSAIC_GPL_CAPS so that applications can
+  tell at compile time that these capability bits exist.
+
+./configure:
+  Unpack the packs into the LibRaw source directory (or anywhere) and use
+    --enable-demosaic-pack-gpl2[=DIR]  (default DIR: $srcdir/LibRaw-demosaic-pack-GPL2)
+    --enable-demosaic-pack-gpl3[=DIR]  (default DIR: $srcdir/LibRaw-demosaic-pack-GPL3)
+  Both are disabled by default; configure fails if an enabled pack is not
+  found. "make check" runs tests/demosaic_test, which checks every user_qual
+  value and the capability bits against the build configuration.
+
+Makefile.devel, Makefile.dist, Makefile.mingw, Makefile.msvc:
+  uncomment the LIBRAW_DEMOSAIC_PACK_GPL2/GPL3 lines (CFLAGSG2/CFLAGSG3 for
+  Makefile.msvc) and adjust the include paths.
+
+Other builds (qmake, Visual Studio project, CMake): add
+  -DLIBRAW_DEMOSAIC_PACK_GPL2 / -DLIBRAW_DEMOSAIC_PACK_GPL3
+and the pack directories to the include path for all library sources.
